course: dictionary
lesson: 10325
title: Old ways and usual ways
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word «traditionally» tells you that something is done in an old way, one that has been passed down for a long time. «Magicians traditionally keep their secrets» means keeping secrets is an old habit of magicians, not a rule someone made last week.
explain: Look at the words around it to be sure. «The kora is a West African instrument... traditionally played by griots, who keep history through song.» The sentence tells you what the griots have always done, so traditionally points to a custom that is old and shared.
explain: The word can also mean usually, as people have long expected. Test it by swapping in usually. If «Magicians usually keep their secrets» still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: Traditionally means in the way that has been done for a long time by a family, group or country.
fact: It can also mean usually, as people have long expected.
fact: «Traditionally» often starts a sentence, as in «Traditionally, ...», and it tells the reader that a custom is old.
fact: «Traditionally eaten», «traditionally made» and «traditionally worn» are phrases you will meet in history and social studies.
fact: A custom can be traditional and still change: «today daughters sometimes do too» shows that an old way is not always the only way.
exercise: «The cinema traditionally shows 24 still pictures, called frames, every second.» What does traditionally mean here? | Only once, on one special day | In a brand-new way invented last year | Very quickly | *In the way that has been done for a long time
exercise: In many French families, «children traditionally leave their shoes by the tree or the fireplace». What do children usually do? | Give their shoes to le Père Noël at school | Hang their stockings on the tree | *Leave their shoes by the tree or the fireplace
exercise: Find one word in «The kora is traditionally played by griots» that tells you the custom is old. | kora | played | *traditionally | griots
test: «Magicians traditionally keep their secrets.» Which word could replace traditionally without changing the meaning? | quietly | never | *usually | suddenly
test: What does a traditionally made gift mean? | *Made the way people have made it for a long time | Made without any tools | Made as a surprise for one person | Made by a robot last week
exam: «Magicians traditionally keep their secrets, so keeping your trick's secret is fine and not a lie.» What does traditionally show here? | *An old custom that people have long followed | A custom that nobody has ever followed | A fact about the weather | A rule that was made only last year
